/*
	Regression: a host-supplied case value under a range the source fixes. Impala cannot tell whether the host's
	value falls inside the window. One below it pasted a negative offset into the label text, and the module failed
	to load with the cryptic `Invalid identifier: .s0.-1`. It is a host bug, so the load must still stop, but now
	with a sentence: a deferred `! FAIL` ahead of the label. (A host-supplied RANGE is different: there a case can
	fall outside a narrowed window legitimately, and its label is skipped. See `switchWindow.impala`.)

	What the golden pins: one `! LSSi` + `! FAIL` per host-supplied case value, none for a literal one.
	Expected (GAZLCmd switchSymbolicCase.gazl main K_LOW 0 K_IN 2 K_HIGH 7): 11 22 99 33
	Expected load failure (GAZLCmd switchSymbolicCase.gazl main K_LOW -1 K_IN 2 K_HIGH 7): case K_LOW is below the start of its switch range (0)
*/
const int DEBUG = 0
extern native printInt
extern native printLF

const int K_LOW;
const int K_IN;
const int K_HIGH;

function pick(int x) returns int r
{
	r = 0;
	switch (x == 0 to 4) {
		case K_LOW: r = 11;
		case K_IN: r = 22;
		case K_HIGH: r = 77;
		case 3: r = 33;
		default: r = 99;
	}
}

function main()
{
	printInt(pick(0)); printLF();
	printInt(pick(2)); printLF();
	printInt(pick(7)); printLF();
	printInt(pick(3)); printLF();
}
